alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The font_shape_oracle entry, invoked as `font_shape_oracle FONT... CASES` with every path relative to the working directory: one to 65536 fonts, then the case file that tests/font/shape_oracle.py writes. It loads each FONT once with load_face, in order, and then reads the case file. Each case in it is a line `FONT SCRIPT COUNT` of three decimal numbers of 1 to 18 digits separated by single spaces, FONT indexing the fonts from 0 and SCRIPT indexing Common, Latin, Greek and Cyrillic from 0, and then a line of COUNT values of 1 to 8 lowercase hexadecimal digits separated by single spaces, empty for none; every line ends with a line feed, and a case of any other shape, or whose FONT or SCRIPT names no font or script, is malformed. For each case it runs shape_run with that font and script over exactly those COUNT values as u32, values that are not Unicode scalar values included, and prints one line: a JSON array holding `[GLYPH, CLUSTER, X_ADVANCE, Y_ADVANCE, X_OFFSET, Y_OFFSET]` in decimal for each ShapedGlyph, in the order shape_run returns them, items separated by a comma and a space; the JSON string `\"driver: too large\"` when shape_run returns TooLarge; or, without calling shape_run, the JSON string `\"driver: case too large\"` when COUNT is past the 16777216 values it accepts. It exits with 0 after printing every case. It exits with 2, with a message on standard error, when the arguments name no font or more than 65536, a FONT or the case file cannot be read, a FONT is longer than the 268435456 bytes load_face accepts or load_face refuses it, standard output refuses a write, or a case is malformed, which it reports after printing the lines of the cases before it.";
